`Layer2D_Document.Dispose()` was already calling `.Dispose()` on all child document objects, but none of those classes implemented `IDisposable`, causing build errors.

## Changes

- **`Object2D_Document`** — implements `IDisposable` with a `virtual void Dispose()` (no-op default). All derived document classes (`Line2D_Document`, `Circle2D_Document`, `Polygon2D_Document`, `Arrow2D_Document`, `Text2D_Document`, `Arc2D_Document`, `Graph2D_Document`, `MathGraph2D_Document`, `Image2D_Document`, `Point2D_Document`) inherit this automatically.

- **`Group2D_Document`** — overrides `Dispose()` to recursively dispose each `Object2D_Document` held in `ObjectList`, then clears the list.

```csharp
// Object2D_Document
public class Object2D_Document : IDisposable
{
    public virtual void Dispose() { }
}

// Group2D_Document
public override void Dispose()
{
    foreach (var item in ObjectList)
        item.Object?.Dispose();
    ObjectList.Clear();
}
```

