Adds `#regionals`, `#regionals/overall`, and `#regionals/$weekNum` route support for regional events (`event_type === 0`), mirroring the district routes pattern from #5. Also adds a fixed "Regionals" entry to the "Jump to District" dropdown.

## Routing
- `#regionals` → `viewRegionalsHome` — regional events grouped by week with "Jump to Week" selector and "Overall Regionals" button
- `#regionals/overall` → `viewRegionalsOverall` — season aggregate across all regionals, grouped by week
- `#regionals/$weekNum` → `viewRegionalsWeek` — per-event aggregate for a single week, with live refresh

## Home page dropdown
- `onchange` now sets `location.hash` directly from option values (full hash strings like `#district/2025ne`)
- Static "Regionals" option always visible; dynamic district options populated as `#district/${key}`
- Removed hide-on-empty-districts logic — dropdown stays visible since "Regionals" is always present

```js
if (page === 'regionals') {
  if (parts[1] === 'overall') return viewRegionalsOverall(CURRENT_YEAR);
  if (parts[1]) return viewRegionalsWeek(CURRENT_YEAR, parts[1] === 'cmp' ? 'cmp' : parseInt(parts[1], 10));
  return viewRegionalsHome(CURRENT_YEAR);
}
```

Renames three exported functions to better reflect their intent, with adjusted signatures where appropriate.

## Changes

- **`doesUrlMatchPatterns(url, ...patterns)`** → **`testPatterns(url, patterns[])`** — accepts an array as the second argument
- **`findMatchingPatterns(url, ...patterns)`** → **`getMatchingPatterns(url, patterns[])`** — takes an array instead of variadic args; name unambiguously describes returning matched patterns
- **`excludeDuplicatePatterns(patterns[])`** → **`removeRedundantPatterns(patterns[])`** — name unambiguously describes removing patterns already covered by broader ones

## Example

```js
// Before
doesUrlMatchPatterns('https://google.com/', 'https://*.google.com/*', '*://example.com/*');
findMatchingPatterns('https://google.com/', 'https://*.google.com/*', '*://example.com/*');
excludeDuplicatePatterns(['https://*.google.com/*', 'https://google.com/*']);

// After
testPatterns('https://google.com/', ['https://*.google.com/*', '*://example.com/*']);
getMatchingPatterns('https://google.com/', ['https://*.google.com/*', '*://example.com/*']);
removeRedundantPatterns(['https://*.google.com/*', 'https://google.com/*']);
```

Tests and README updated accordingly.

On tablet and desktop, the scroll-to-top button was stacked *above* the WhatsApp floating button (higher `bottom` value), inconsistent with mobile where it correctly sits below.

## Changes

- **Desktop (≥769px):** Swapped `bottom` values — WA circle raised to `4.75rem`, back-to-top lowered to `1.75rem`
- **Tablet (≤768px):** Swapped `bottom` values — WA pill raised to `4rem`, back-to-top lowered to `1rem`

```css
/* Before */
.floating-wa  { bottom: 1.75rem; }   /* desktop */
.back-to-top  { bottom: 4.75rem; }

/* After */
.floating-wa  { bottom: 4.75rem; }
.back-to-top  { bottom: 1.75rem; }
```

Mobile (≤480px) was already correct and is unchanged.
